    affiliation: "Renault SAS"
  - family-names: Martinez
    given-names: John-Jairo
    affiliation: "Univ. Grenoble Alpes, CNRS, Grenoble INP, GIPSA-lab"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/<your-username>/LPV-YK-Control"
abstract: >-
  MATLAB reference implementation of two LPV-Youla-Kucera control
  architectures that guarantee smooth, unconstrained switching between
  multiple independently designed LPV controllers: a grid-based scheme
  using parameter-dependent Lyapunov certificates, and a partitioned
  polytopic scheme using trajectory-aligned convex subsets with shared
  boundary controllers. Validated experimentally on the lateral control
  of an autonomous Renault ZOE.
keywords:
  - linear parameter-varying
  - Youla-Kucera parametrization
  - switching control
  - robust control
  - linear matrix inequalities
  - autonomous vehicles
  - lateral control
